      "parameters": {
        "jsonSchemaExample": "{\n  \"UID\": \"111220251\",\n  \"Name\": \"John Tan Wei Ming\",\n  \"Department\": \"Human Resource (HR)\",\n  \"Request Type\": \"Daily Report ,Automation\",\n  \"Usual Time Taken\": \"45 minutes daily\",\n  \"Source Data\": \"HRIQ portal attendance data, Excel attachments\",\n\"Deliverables\": \"Formatted Excel report with summary metrics, emailed to managers\",\n  \"Details of workflow\": \"Automated Daily Attendance Summary Processing\\nManual Process:\\n1. HR downloads raw attendance data from the HRIQ portal.\\n2. Opens Excel and cleans data (remove duplicates, format dates, update missing fields).\\n3. Computes workers present, workers on leave, forgot to clock out, regular hours and OT hours.\\n4. Cross-checks against Masterlist.\\n5. Formats final report with summary totals.\\n6. Emails file to Operations Manager and Supervisors.\\n\\nAutomated Process (n8n):\\n1. Trigger daily at 6:00 AM.\\n2. IMAP node checks mailbox for new “Attendance Report”.\\n3. Download and parse Excel into JSON.\\n4. Clean data (normalize dates, fix time formats, remove duplicates).\\n5. Apply logic (forgot to clock out, working flag, leave status, total hours + OT).\\n6. Generate output (Masterdata sheet, pivot summary, formulas, formatting).\\n7. Upload to Google Drive.\\n8. Email final report to HR & Operations.\\n\\nOutcome: Manual time 45 minutes → automated 10 seconds, reduced errors, consistent formatting.\",\n  \"Solution to digitalize the process\":\"Using AI tools to help download the file from HRIQ, format the report using python's pandas library and also create the pivot table from the report itself. Use SMTP to automatically send out the email after the report is created successfully\"\n}",
        "autoFix": true
      },
